      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.contextHeading">Context</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.overview">[PLACEHOLDER OVERVIEW — EDIT ME] Operational case study: design and implementation of an AI-assisted workflow automation system for an engineering company, integrating document ingestion, AI-assisted processing, structured databases, and human validation points.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-problem-solution reveal">
        <div class="problem-card">
          <h3 data-i18n="project.problemHeading">Problem</h3>
          <p data-i18n="project7.problem">[PLACEHOLDER] Repetitive manual work in document handling, reporting, and internal communication was consuming engineering hours and slowing delivery.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="solution-card">
          <h3 data-i18n="project.solutionHeading">Solution</h3>
          <p data-i18n="project7.solution">[PLACEHOLDER] AI-assisted ingestion + structured extraction + human-in-the-loop validation + automated report generation + cloud storage with structured paths.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.problemContextHeading">Existing context</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.problemContext">[PLACEHOLDER] The company's project intake, reporting and document distribution relied on manual copy-paste between email, spreadsheets and shared folders.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.problemWorkflowHeading">Current manual workflow</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.problemWorkflow">[PLACEHOLDER] 1. Operator receives documents by email or upload. 2. Manual classification. 3. Manual data extraction into spreadsheets. 4. Manual formatting of reports. 5. Manual email distribution. 6. Manual filing.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.problemBottlenecksHeading">Identified bottlenecks</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.problemBottlenecks">[PLACEHOLDER] Manual data entry (slow, error-prone), version control of spreadsheets (no audit trail), report formatting (high variability between operators), knowledge loss when staff changes.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.solutionArchHeading">Automation architecture</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.solutionArch">[PLACEHOLDER] n8n orchestrator pulling from email/cloud storage, sending documents to OCR + LLM pipeline, extracting structured fields, storing into a structured database, generating standardized reports via templates, notifying human validators, archiving in versioned folder.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.solutionAIHeading">AI components</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.solutionAI">[PLACEHOLDER] Cloud LLM for structured extraction (frontier model), local LLM as fallback for sensitive documents, OCR service for scanned inputs, embeddings for semantic search across the document archive.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.solutionHumanHeading">Human validation points</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.solutionHuman">[PLACEHOLDER] Every extracted record passes through a human-in-the-loop validation step before being committed to the structured database. Edge cases are flagged for review, not auto-accepted.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.techHeading">Tools used</h2>
        <ul class="chips" role="list">
          <li class="chip">n8n</li><li class="chip">Cloud LLM (frontier)</li><li class="chip">Local LLM</li><li class="chip">OCR</li><li class="chip">Telegram bot</li><li class="chip">Cloud VPS</li><li class="chip">Microsoft Office automation</li><li class="chip">Structured database</li><li class="chip">Cloud storage</li><li class="chip">API integrations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.securityHeading">Security considerations</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.security">[PLACEHOLDER] Local LLM for documents flagged as sensitive; encryption at rest in cloud storage; least-privilege access; audit logs of every automation run; no document content sent to third-party APIs without explicit classification.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.stagesHeading">Implementation stages</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.stages">Stage 1: workflow discovery & process mapping. Stage 2: pilot on a single document class. Stage 3: structured database schema. Stage 4: full automation pipeline. Stage 5: human validation UI. Stage 6: report templates. Stage 7: rollout to operators. Stage 8: measurement & tuning.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.timeSavedHeading">Time saved</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.timeSaved">[TBD — to be added] hours per week</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.manualReducedHeading">Manual steps reduced</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.manualReduced">[TBD — to be added] manual steps eliminated per intake</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.timeImprovementHeading">Processing time improvement</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.timeImprovement">[TBD — to be added]% reduction in processing time</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.errorReductionHeading">Error reduction</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.errorReduction">[TBD — to be added]% reduction in extraction errors (measured vs manual baseline)</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.scalabilityHeading">Scalability</h2>
        <div class="impact-card"><p data-i18n="project7.scalability">The pattern scales horizontally: adding a new document class requires a new extraction schema and validation rule — no rewrite of the pipeline.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.impactHeading">Business impact</h2>
        <div class="impact-card"><p data-i18n="project7.impact">[PLACEHOLDER] Repetitive low-value work removed from engineering workflows, allowing professionals to focus on decisions and expertise. Standardized reporting reduces variability between operators. Audit trail introduced where there was none.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.lessonsHeading">Lessons learned</h2>
        <div class="lessons-card"><p data-i18n="project7.lessons">[PLACEHOLDER] Human-in-the-loop is non-negotiable for high-stakes records. Structured outputs from LLMs require schema validation. Edge cases are the most informative for tuning. Document the workflow before automating it.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section reveal">
        <h2 data-i18n="project.futureHeading">Future development</h2>
        <p data-i18n="project7.future">[PLACEHOLDER] Additional document classes, semantic search across the archive, predictive prioritization of incoming items, full bilingual EN/RO support in the validation UI.</p>
      </div>

